00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.110 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  Thank You Bernadette ah and ladies and  gentlemen I can tell just breathing this  hair that you have had a very productive  day behind you so thank you for having  me in thank you to the Global Covenant  of Mayors for inviting me to speak at  the closing session today you have had a  lively discussions on the role of cities  and actions taken at local level to  promote clean energy and the transition  towards climate neutral economy you are  at the core of the transition effective  urban planning good local practices  micro financing and small-scale  innovation are essential to deliver on  the Paris agreement goals last Monday  the President of the European Commission  ocean Amanda Lyon presented the EU  ambition to make Europe the first  climate neutral continent by 2050 and in  two days the European Commission will  lay out their European clean deed and  agenda to make Europe cleaner and  cleaner but also with a more competitive  and resilient economy there are many  drivers for the European Green Deal but  I believe people better consumers or  producers of energy or workers or the  real driver of the change towards  climate neutrality well either the  European Green Deal will work for all or  it will not work at all every household  SME or industry should be able to  benefit from affordable secure and clean  and I chip each of them should be able  to express its concerns and proposals  and propose its ideas on how to make  climate neutrality happen the Global  Covenant of Mayors provides an ideal  platform to keep people center stage and  currently their voices heard in the past  year so you have seen an unprecedented  scale of  engagement at the local level local  authorities mayor's are best placed to  speak to citizens and rely their  concerns at national and European level  it would be a historical mistake to  imagine that the clean deal will be a  top-down agendas right driven by  Brussels it must closely involved  citizens through dialogue at local level  the Covenant of Mayors will have a  central role not only to providing forum  for any changes of good practices  practices but also to implement changes  locally every sector will have to  contribute and energy plays a central  role in T carburizing our economy Europe  has succeeded to get to 31 percent of  electricity produced from renewable  renewable sources and more than half  comes from low-carbon technologies and  cities will be around the table with  central governments and regional  authorities when developing the plans to  get Europe to its climate and energy  goals this is where I see the Covenant  of Mayors bringing bringing its ambition  experience and networks of cities to  contribute to the process finally I will  apply the same principles on which a  Green Deal is based in Europe also to  our global action climate transition  must be just and it must be democratic  since I have started my mandate only  last week but I already have met many  international partners and organizations  and I will put trade and I will put at  the center of my actions the external  dimension of energy policy because EU  only accounts for 9% of the global  emissions we can lead the way but we  cannot succeed unless we bring along our  partners our major international  partners and our closest neighbors and  that is why the Global Covenant is so  important for me today City diplomacy is  growing ever stronger and the global  covenant cities see  networks and partners are the key driver  for a change  the Commission is fully committed to  help the global covenant to step up its  work this means supporting the global  governance Secretariat as well as the  network of regional governance around  the world and it is with cities that  were either succeed or fail in  implementing the clean energy transition  so we are partners in achieving our  climate neutral world thank you for your  efforts and let us take global  governance to the next level thank you  [Applause]

